## The trade-offs are real

- **The package family is pre-1.0.** APIs move, so scaffolded imports use exact
  `{{ releaseSpecifier }}` pins. If you need a frozen surface today, wait or budget for upgrades.
- **The .NET Aspire CLI is the default orchestration path.** Scaffold with `--no-aspire` to opt out;
  resource wiring and local telemetry then belong to you. [See the Aspire boundary](/quickstart/aspire/).
- **The web layer is Fresh and Preact.** That is a deliberate fit, not compatibility with the
  React/Next ecosystem. [See the web layer](/web-layer/).
- **A coordinated workspace is broader than a one-process app needs.** A small service pays the
  structure cost before durable work, plugins, and multi-resource operations pay it back.
- **NetScript is not a hosted platform.** You own the workspace and the deployment decisions.

If those are the problems and trade-offs you recognize, [start the workspace](/quickstart/).
